const faqs = [
  { q: "Can I get a loan against an Argyle pink diamond?", a: "Potentially. ALYRA considers diamonds and high-value jewellery as security for asset-based loans. Whether a particular Argyle pink diamond is suitable depends on its authenticity, condition, valuation, documentation, market demand, custody requirements and the applicable loan terms." },
  { q: "How much can I borrow against my Argyle pink diamond?", a: "There is no single amount that applies to every Argyle pink diamond. ALYRA assesses each eligible asset individually and provides a written loan offer only after specialist assessment, subject to valuation, approval, custody, documentation and agreed loan terms." },
  { q: "What makes an Argyle pink diamond valuable?", a: "Important characteristics include colour, carat weight, clarity and cut, together with Argyle provenance and supporting documentation. GIA identifies colour as the dominant value factor for fancy-colour diamonds, while larger stones are generally rarer than smaller examples." },
  { q: "How do I prove my pink diamond is from Argyle?", a: "Start with the diamond's Argyle documentation and laser inscription. Argyle's Diamond Check service is intended to confirm whether an eligible laser number corresponds with a record in the Argyle Pink Diamonds database. Argyle also operates a Gem Analysis Service for qualifying stones, although that service differs from the original Chain of Custody certification programme." },
  { q: "Do I need a GIA report?", a: "An independent grading report can provide important information about a coloured diamond, including whether its colour is natural or treated and its colour grade and clarity. The appropriate documentation will depend on the individual stone and the information already available." },
  { q: "Can I borrow against an Argyle pink diamond ring?", a: "Potentially. ALYRA considers jewellery, coloured stones and loose diamonds as eligible asset categories, subject to specialist assessment. The asset is reviewed for factors including condition, documents, value, authenticity and market demand." },
  { q: "Does ALYRA hold my Argyle pink diamond during the loan?", a: "Yes. If the loan proceeds, ALYRA holds the diamond securely as security for the agreed loan term. You remain the owner of the diamond while the loan is active. Once the loan has been repaid in accordance with the agreed terms, ALYRA returns the diamond to you." },
  { q: "Is my diamond sold while the loan is active?", a: "No public listing, auction campaign or marketplace sale is required while the loan is proceeding normally. ALYRA holds the asset as security during the loan term. The asset is at risk, however, if the repayment obligations in the loan agreement are not met." },
